      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Logistic Regression Training set shape: (1070, 8)\n",
            "Logistic Regression Testing set shape: (268, 8)\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4a8a2437"
      },
      "source": [
        "It's good practice to scale the numerical features before training a Logistic Regression model, especially when using regularization, to ensure that no single feature dominates the learning process due to its scale. We will use `StandardScaler`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "fe5d7449",
        "outputId": "ba43f96b-007e-4785-e249-e09d2f0fdf8c"
      },
      "source": [
        "scaler_logistic = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_train_logistic_scaled = scaler_logistic.fit_transform(X_train_logistic)\n",
        "X_test_logistic_scaled = scaler_logistic.transform(X_test_logistic)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Features scaled for Logistic Regression.\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Features scaled for Logistic Regression.\n"
